                <pb facs="1782" n="1582" sameAs="frus:frus1945Berlinv02/pg1582"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#small-caps">Editor’s Note</hi></head>
                <p>—The two memoranda printed in this appendix were prepared by Charles E. Bohlen in March 1960 on the basis of
                    his original longhand notes of two Truman–Stalin meetings
                    at the Berlin Conference and from memory, in view of the fact that the editors
                    were unable to find the memoranda of conversation which Bohlen is certain he transcribed in July 1945.
                    For literal transcripts of the original longhand notes referred to, see <hi
                        rendition="#italic">ante</hi>, <ref target="#pg43">pp. 43</ref>–<ref
                        target="#pg46">46</ref>, <ref target="#pg87">87</ref>. With respect to these
                    later reconstructions of the Truman-Stalin meetings
                    of July 17 and 18, 1945, Bohlen has made
                    the following explanatory comment: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“I made no attempt to reproduce the actual words during these interviews,
                            since the notes are too fragmentary to ensure any accuracy even with the
                            exercise of memory. Rather, I have sought to deal in narrative form with
                            the subjects covered.”</p>
                    </quote></p>
            </div>
